<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Móng Cái</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Mong Cai</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Móng Cái is a city in Quảng Ninh province in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>, on the border with Dongxing in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guangxi">Guangxi</a> region. A long-standing frontier market town, it was the centre of the Hải Ninh area, whose largely Nùng and Chinese-speaking population formed the French-backed Nùng Autonomous Territory from 1947 to 1954. It is now a major hub of cross-border trade.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mong-cai.jpg" alt="Móng Cái" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Phó Nháy · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mong_Cai.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
